# Governance Proposal: Add Free Fleet Card to Dashboard

**Proposer:** Ganesha (Claude Code CLI)
**Date:** 2026-02-28T18:40:00Z
**Type:** Code Enhancement
**Trust Level:** ENGINEER (3)

## Summary
The SAFE dashboard has no visibility into the free fleet (14 LLM providers). This proposal adds a "Free Fleet" status card that calls `/api/fleet/providers` and shows how many providers are active and their names.

## Proposed Changes
**File:** `SAFE/web/dashboard.html`
**Location:** Two insertions: (1) HTML card after Google card, (2) JS renderFleet() after renderGoogle(), (3) call in DOMContentLoaded

## Rationale
- Users and operators have no visibility into fleet health from the dashboard
- `/api/fleet/providers` endpoint exists and returns correct data
- Follows identical pattern to existing status cards

## Risk Assessment
- **Risk Level:** MINIMAL
- **Reversible:** YES
- **Dependencies:** Willow server on port 8420
- **Testing:** Open dashboard, fleet card should show provider count

## ΔE Impact
Expected ΔE: +0.008 (fleet visibility)

## Implementation
```python
from pathlib import Path

target = Path(r"C:\Users\Sean\Documents\GitHub\SAFE\web\dashboard.html")
content = target.read_text(encoding="utf-8")

# 1. Add fleet card HTML after Google card (before Willow Server card)
old_html = '''      <div class="status-card">
        <div class="card-label">Willow Server</div>'''
new_html = '''      <div class="status-card">
        <div class="card-label">Free Fleet</div>
        <div class="card-status" id="fleetStatus">&mdash;</div>
        <div class="card-detail" id="fleetDetail"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="status-card">
        <div class="card-label">Willow Server</div>'''
content = content.replace(old_html, new_html, 1)

# 2. Add renderFleet() JS after renderGoogle() function
old_js = '''// ── Render: Finish Prompt ────────────────────────────────────────────────────'''
new_js = '''// ── Render: Free Fleet card ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

async function renderFleet() {
  const statusEl = document.getElementById('fleetStatus');
  const detailEl = document.getElementById('fleetDetail');
  if (!statusEl) return;
  try {
    const res = await fetch('http://localhost:8420/api/fleet/providers');
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(res.status);
    const data = await res.json();
    const active = data.active || 0;
    const total = data.total || 0;
    if (active > 0) {
      statusEl.innerHTML = '<span class="status-dot-green"></span>' + active + ' of ' + total + ' providers active';
      statusEl.style.color = '';
      const names = (data.providers || []).filter(p => p.active).map(p => p.name).join(', ');
      detailEl.textContent = names;
    } else {
      statusEl.textContent = 'No fleet providers active';
      statusEl.style.color = 'var(--fg-muted)';
      detailEl.textContent = '';
    }
  } catch (e) {
    statusEl.textContent = 'Fleet unavailable';
    statusEl.style.color = 'var(--fg-muted)';
    detailEl.textContent = '';
  }
}

// ── Render: Finish Prompt ────────────────────────────────────────────────────'''
content = content.replace(old_js, new_js, 1)

# 3. Add renderFleet() call in DOMContentLoaded after renderGoogle(acct)
old_call = '''  renderGoogle(acct);
  renderFinishPrompt(acct);'''
new_call = '''  renderGoogle(acct);
  renderFleet();
  renderFinishPrompt(acct);'''
content = content.replace(old_call, new_call, 1)

target.write_text(content, encoding="utf-8")
print(f"Written: {target}")

# Verify insertions
assert 'fleetStatus' in content, "fleet card HTML missing"
assert 'renderFleet' in content, "renderFleet function missing"
assert 'renderFleet()' in content, "renderFleet call missing"
print("All 3 insertions verified.")
```

